mind means a new analysis, not a quiet edit.

## Goal
Do the samples separate by condition (untreated vs treated) in the major axes of variation of
the gene expression data? A principal component analysis of the gene count matrix, with samples
plotted in PC space and coloured by condition.

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| `counts_gene` | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper (native) | `02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv` |
| `design` | 01_prepare_samplesheets (native) | `01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv` |

## Method
Environment: `gars-bio` (pandas 3.0.5, numpy 2.5.2, scikit-learn 1.9.0, matplotlib 3.11.1). Everything
runs in one batch job. Inputs are read-only.

1. Read the count matrix (tab-separated; `gene_id`, `gene_name`, then one column per sample: A1-A3, B1-B3)
   and the design table (`sample_id,condition,group,replicate`). Check that the sample columns and
   `sample_id` match exactly (same 6 samples); stop with an error if not.
2. Transform: `log2(x + 1)` on the length-scaled gene counts (the matrix is not integer-valued,
   which is expected for `gene_counts_length_scaled`).
3. Filter: drop genes with zero variance across samples. No other expression filter is applied.
4. PCA with `sklearn.decomposition.PCA` (full SVD, deterministic) on the samples x genes matrix,
   genes mean-centred, **not** scaled to unit variance. All genes that pass step 3 are used.
   With 6 samples this yields at most 5 components.
5. Write the sample coordinates (all components) joined to `condition`, and the variance explained
   per component.
6. Plot PC1 vs PC2, one point per sample, coloured by `condition`, each point labelled with its
   sample_id, axis labels carrying % variance explained. Fixed colour per condition, legend on.

Choices made here that you may want to change before approving: log2(x+1) rather than a
variance-stabilising transform (the upstream artifact is the only count matrix resolvable, and
DESeq2 VST is not part of this plan); centred-only rather than scaled; all genes rather than the
top N most variable.

